WEBVTT

NOTE
Transcribed from the narration in this video. Every figure the
speaker states matches the OECD time-use data behind this page.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
Bonjour, you want to
know how my day goes?

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.460
Sit down, there's no rush here.

3
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.400
I wake up and I take my time.

4
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.880
Breakfast, a warm croissant,
butter, good coffee.

5
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:15.260
In France, we spend 12 hours and 32
minutes a day just on personal care.

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.600
We believe the body
deserves attention.

7
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.680
Then I work, but not like crazy.

8
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.260
I do about three hours and 24
minutes of paid work a day.

9
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.000
We work around 1,487 hours a year.

10
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.840
Enough to live, not
enough to forget how to.

11
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.280
After that, there's
the invisible work.

12
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.700
Cooking a real meal, tidying up,
maybe helping a neighbour.

13
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.400
I do about three
hours of unpaid work.

14
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.080
And then, leisure,
almost five hours of it.

15
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.840
I read, I walk, I sit at a café and
watch people argue about cheese.

16
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:50.400
Four hours and 53
minutes every single day.

17
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.960
I get 74 entire 24-hour
days of free time a year.

18
00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.600
Oh, and the best part?

19
00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.060
Most of us retire by 61.

20
00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.960
You see, in France,
the day is not a race.

21
00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.000
It's a meal.

22
00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.680
And we take every course.

23
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.480
That's my day in France.

24
00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.568
Au revoir.
